# `let s = "\("\(n)")"` - interpolation inside interpolation.
#
# The `"` at byte 21 opens a new literal rather than closing the one at 18,
# and a hand with no memory across the body cannot tell those apart.
# Outer [18, 29), inner [21, 27).
roots 1
mends 0
holds line_string_literal
spans line_string_literal 18 29
spans line_string_literal 21 27
